Falsifies `elf::note::verification::note_segments_from_a_head_never_panic`.

The defect: the program header table's end is computed but never compared with the bytes the reader
holds. The shell hands this function one page of a file anyone may have written, and a `phoff` or
`phnum` that points past that page then slices outside it.

Expected to fail: a slice index out of range in `NoteSegments::from_head`.

